IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mair-dates`
IMPORT `mair-core`

-- Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018 (Qld) -- the provisions a claimant meets, from the seat of the claimant.
--
-- SEAT: the claimant: the person injured in a motor vehicle accident in Queensland who claims damages under the Motor
-- Accident Insurance Act 1994, or the person claiming for them or, for a death, for the dependants. "What must my
-- notice of claim say, and what goes with it? Is my disability significant? Does my identity evidence do? Can my claim
-- be settled, and does the insurer have to explain its offer? Will the insurer pay my expenses now? By when must it give
-- me what it learns about me? What costs do I get if I accept a mandatory final offer?" Every question is asked as the
-- claimant would ask it, on facts the claimant can state; the insurer's, the court's and the public trustee's
-- decisions are facts the claimant answers from what they have been told. The rules are in mair-core.l4; this module
-- builds their inputs from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the same meaning have the same name in every
-- question.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018 -- the claimant's questions`

DECLARE `Mobility device answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Nominal Defendant provides gratuitous insurance for motorised mobility devices (s 14)`
    `s 14 does not say: it covers only motorised mobility devices`

DECLARE `Capacity assumption answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the insurer may assume I am of full capacity (s 20(3))`
    `no: the insurer may not assume I am of full capacity (s 20(3))`
    `s 20(3) does not say: it is about adult claimants only`

DECLARE `Expenses answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: my request meets s 21`
    `no: my request does not meet s 21`
    `s 21 does not say: it covers only private hospital, medical, pharmaceutical and rehabilitation expenses`

DECLARE `Information answer` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer has until this day to give me the information (s 22(1))` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the insurer gave me the information in time (s 22(1))`
    `the insurer is late: the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the insurer may withhold it if it has reasonable grounds to suspect me of fraud, and must then tell the commission within 1 month (s 22(2)-(3))`

DECLARE `Costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `s 29 does not set my costs: the offer was not accepted, or was not more than the lower offer limit, or was more than the upper offer limit`

DECLARE `Examination answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: allowances and expenses on the same basis as a District Court witness (s 30)`
    `s 30 does not say: it covers only a person required to attend for examination under Part 5B of the Act`

§§ `Who insures a motorised mobility device (s 14)`
-- Arises only if a motorised mobility device (such as a mobility scooter) was involved in the accident.

@export Is the motorised mobility device (such as a mobility scooter) involved in my Queensland accident insured by the Nominal Defendant?
GIVEN `the vehicle is a motorised mobility device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle involved is a motorised mobility device as defined in the Transport Operations (Road Use Management) Act 1995, schedule 4 (for example a mobility scooter or motorised wheelchair)
GIVETH A `Mobility device answer`
DECIDE `Is the mobility device insured by the Nominal Defendant` IS
    CONSIDER `gratuitously insured by the Nominal Defendant under s 14` `the vehicle is a motorised mobility device`
    WHEN JUST x THEN `yes: the Nominal Defendant provides gratuitous insurance for motorised mobility devices (s 14)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 14 does not say: it covers only motorised mobility devices`

§§ `The notice of claim (ss 16-19)`

@export What must my Queensland motor accident notice of claim include (Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018, ss 17 and 19)?
GIVEN `I claim for someone else's death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a derivative claim: one based on the death of, or injury to, someone other than you (for example a dependant's claim for a death, or a spouse's claim for loss of consortium)
      `I am employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed
      `the injured person was a passenger or other occupant, not the driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or, for a derivative claim, the injured person) were an occupant of a vehicle in the accident but not its driver
      `a property damage claim has been made on the vehicle I was in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a property damage claim has been made under a comprehensive or third party property damage policy for the vehicle you (or the injured person) were travelling in
      `I consulted a lawyer about claiming` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have consulted a lawyer about the possibility of making a claim
      `I have retained a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have retained a law practice to act for you on the claim
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `What must my notice of claim include` IS
    `what the notice of claim must include (ss 17 and 19)` `I claim for someone else's death or injury` `I am employed` `the injured person was a passenger or other occupant, not the driver` `a property damage claim has been made on the vehicle I was in` `I consulted a lawyer about claiming` `I have retained a law practice`

@export What certificates and documents must go with my Queensland motor accident notice of claim (Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018, s 18)?
GIVEN `I claim for someone else's death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a derivative claim: one based on the death of, or injury to, someone other than you
      `I claim as or for the dependants of someone who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is made by or for the dependants of a person who died as a result of injury in a motor vehicle accident
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in complete years when you give the notice of claim
      `I hold a government-issued document that is evidence of my identity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a document issued by a government that is evidence of your identity (for example a driver licence or passport), current or not
      `that document contains my photograph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that document contains a photograph of you (answer no if you hold no such document)
      `I have retained a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have retained a law practice to act for you on the claim
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `What must go with my notice of claim` IS
    `what must accompany the notice of claim (s 18)` `I claim for someone else's death or injury` `I claim as or for the dependants of someone who died` `my age in years` (`is an identity document (s 18(5))` `I hold a government-issued document that is evidence of my identity` `that document contains my photograph`) `I have retained a law practice`

@export Is my Queensland motor accident notice of claim in the form s 16 of the Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018 requires?
GIVEN `my notice is in the commission's approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice of claim is in the form approved by the Motor Accident Insurance Commission
      `my notice is signed and witnessed as the form shows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is signed and witnessed as shown in the form
      `the form says some information must be verified on oath` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the form states that some or all of your information must be verified by you on oath
      `the oath is completed by me and a person permitted to administer it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the oath on the form is completed, as the form shows, by you and by a person permitted by law to administer oaths (answer no if there is no oath)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my notice in the required form` IS
    `the notice meets s 16` `my notice is in the commission's approved form` `my notice is signed and witnessed as the form shows` `the form says some information must be verified on oath` `the oath is completed by me and a person permitted to administer it`

@export Is my disability (an injury, illness or other disability) significant, so that I must list it, and the claims and payments for it, in my Queensland motor accident notice of claim?
GIVEN `the disability may be relevant to assessing my injury from the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disability may be relevant to assessing the extent of the injury you suffered in the accident (for example an earlier injury to the same part of the body)
      `the days the disability or its symptoms lasted` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days the disability or its symptoms lasted (or have lasted so far)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disability significant` IS
    `the disability is significant (s 17(3))` `the disability may be relevant to assessing my injury from the accident` `the days the disability or its symptoms lasted`

@export Does the identity evidence I give with my Queensland motor accident notice of claim meet s 18(4) of the Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in complete years when you give the notice of claim
      `I hold a government-issued document that is evidence of my identity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a document issued by a government that is evidence of your identity (for example a driver licence or passport), current or not
      `that document contains my photograph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that document contains a photograph of you (answer no if you hold no such document)
      `that document is current` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that document is current, not expired (answer no if you hold no such document)
      `who certified my copy as a true copy` IS A `Certifier` @desc Who certified your copy of the identity document to be a true copy: a lawyer, a notary public, a commissioner for declarations, a justice of the peace, or someone else or nobody
      `my photograph is passport-size` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you give a photograph instead: whether it is passport-size (answer no if you give none)
      `the day my photograph was taken` IS A DATE @desc If you give a photograph: the day it was taken (any date if you give none)
      `the day I give the notice of claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you give the notice of claim to the insurer
      `the person who certified my photograph has known me since` IS A DATE @desc If you give a photograph: the day from which the person certifying it as a photograph of you has known you (any date if you give none)
      `the day my photograph was certified` IS A DATE @desc If you give a photograph: the day it was certified (any date if you give none)
GIVETH AN `Identity evidence answer`
DECIDE `Does my identity evidence meet s 18(4)` IS
    `the s 18(4) answer` `my age in years` (`is an identity document (s 18(5))` `I hold a government-issued document that is evidence of my identity` `that document contains my photograph`) `that document is current` (`is a certified copy (s 18(5))` `who certified my copy as a true copy`) (`is a recent certified photograph (s 18(5))` `my photograph is passport-size` `the day my photograph was taken` `the day I give the notice of claim` `the person who certified my photograph has known me since` `the day my photograph was certified`)

@export Does what my law practice gave someone for referring me count as consideration, which my claimant's certificate must address (Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018, s 18(2)(c) and (5))?
GIVEN `the kind of benefit given for the referral` IS A `Referral benefit` @desc What was given for referring you to the law practice: money; a gift other than money; hospitality; or another fee or benefit
      `its value in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc Its value in Australian dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the referral benefit consideration` IS
    `is consideration (s 18(5))` `the kind of benefit given for the referral` `its value in dollars`

§§ `Settling the claim (s 20)`

@export Must the insurer's offer of settlement to me come with an explanatory statement in the commission's approved form?
GIVEN `a lawyer represents me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a lawyer represents you on the claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the offer come with an explanatory statement` IS
    `the insurer's offer must come with an explanatory statement (s 20(1))` `a lawyer represents me`

@export Can an offer or counteroffer of settlement of my Queensland motor accident claim be made or accepted by or for me, or does it first need the court's or the public trustee's approval?
GIVEN `I am an adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (the claimant) are 18 or older
      `I am of full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to manage your own affairs, including the claim
      `the court or public trustee is satisfied the settlement is in my best interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court or the public trustee has said it is satisfied that settling on the proposed terms would be in your best interests
      `the court or public trustee has approved the terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court or the public trustee has approved the terms of the offer or counteroffer
GIVETH A `Settlement answer`
DECIDE `Can my claim be settled` IS
    `the s 20(2) answer` `I am an adult` `I am of full legal capacity` `the court or public trustee is satisfied the settlement is in my best interests` `the court or public trustee has approved the terms`

@export May the insurer assume that I am of full capacity when it negotiates settlement of my Queensland motor accident claim?
GIVEN `I am an adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (the claimant) are 18 or older
      `my mental incapacity is obvious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a mental incapacity that is obvious and should be apparent to the insurer
      `I am under a protection order under the Public Trustee Act 1978` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are subject to a protection order under the Public Trustee Act 1978 (Qld)
      `the court has declared me under its protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has declared you to be under its protection in negotiating settlement of the claim
GIVETH A `Capacity assumption answer`
DECIDE `May the insurer assume I have full capacity` IS
    CONSIDER `the insurer may assume full capacity (s 20(3))` `I am an adult` `my mental incapacity is obvious` `I am under a protection order under the Public Trustee Act 1978` `the court has declared me under its protection`
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x THEN `yes: the insurer may assume I am of full capacity (s 20(3))` ELSE `no: the insurer may not assume I am of full capacity (s 20(3))`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 20(3) does not say: it is about adult claimants only`

@export Can the court declare me to be under its protection in negotiating settlement of my Queensland motor accident claim?
GIVEN `an interested person has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone with an interest (for example a family member) has applied to the court for the declaration
      `I cannot manage my affairs or resist undue influence because of illness, infirmity or drugs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are permanently or intermittently unable to manage your affairs, or to resist undue influence, because of physical or mental illness or infirmity, or the influence of drugs
      `the court finds I need its protection for another reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds you need its protection for some other reason
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court put me under its protection` IS
    `the court may declare the claimant under its protection (s 20(4))` `an interested person has applied to the court` `I cannot manage my affairs or resist undue influence because of illness, infirmity or drugs` `the court finds I need its protection for another reason`

§§ `Treatment and rehabilitation expenses (s 21)`

@export Does my request to the insurer to pay or reimburse my treatment or rehabilitation expenses meet the $200 minimum and evidence rules (Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018, s 21)?
GIVEN `the kind of expenses` IS AN `Expense kind` @desc Which expenses you ask for: private hospital, medical and pharmaceutical expenses (Act, s 42); rehabilitation expenses (Act, s 51); or other expenses
      `the total I ask for` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount of this request, in Australian dollars
      `I attach receipts, unpaid accounts or other evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request is accompanied by receipts, unpaid accounts or other appropriate evidence of the expenses
      `I expect to make no further request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you expect this to be your last request for payment or reimbursement of expenses
      `the request is for all my outstanding expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request is for the whole outstanding total of your expenses
GIVETH AN `Expenses answer`
DECIDE `Does my expenses request meet s 21` IS
    CONSIDER `the request meets s 21` `the kind of expenses` `the total I ask for` `I attach receipts, unpaid accounts or other evidence` `I expect to make no further request` `the request is for all my outstanding expenses`
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x THEN `yes: my request meets s 21` ELSE `no: my request does not meet s 21`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 21 does not say: it covers only private hospital, medical, pharmaceutical and rehabilitation expenses`

§§ `Information the insurer obtains about me (s 22)`
-- Arises only once the insurer has obtained records about you under the permission in your notice of claim (s 19).

@export By when must the insurer give me information it obtained about me under the records permission in my Queensland motor accident notice of claim, and is it late?
GIVEN `the day the insurer obtained the information` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer obtained the information about you under the permission you gave in your notice of claim (s 19)
      `the insurer has told me it withholds the information on suspicion of fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has told you it is withholding the information because it suspects you of fraud
      `I have received the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you the information
      `the day I received it` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer gave you the information (any date if you have not received it)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Information answer`
DECIDE `By when must the insurer give me the information` IS
    IF `the insurer has told me it withholds the information on suspicion of fraud`
    THEN `the insurer may withhold it if it has reasonable grounds to suspect me of fraud, and must then tell the commission within 1 month (s 22(2)-(3))`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 22 -- the insurer must give the claimant the information within 1 month, unless it withholds it on suspicion of fraud` `the days allowed`) 0 `what has happened`
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the insurer gave me the information in time (s 22(1))`
         OTHERWISE IF `I have received the information` OR `the days allowed` LESS THAN (`the days from` `the day the insurer obtained the information` `to` `today`)
                   THEN `the insurer is late: the last day was` `the last day for it`
                   ELSE `the insurer has until this day to give me the information (s 22(1))` `the last day for it`
    WHERE
        `the last day for it` MEANS `the last day to give the claimant the information (s 22(1))` `the day the insurer obtained the information`
        `the days allowed`    MEANS `the days from` `the day the insurer obtained the information` `to` `the last day for it`
        `what has happened`   MEANS
            IF `I have received the information`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give the claimant the information` (`the days from` `the day the insurer obtained the information` `to` `the day I received it`))
            ELSE LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `ask about the information` (`the days from` `the day the insurer obtained the information` `to` `today`))

§§ `Costs when I accept a mandatory final offer (s 29)`
-- Arises only if the claim was not settled at the compulsory conference and a mandatory final offer was accepted.

@export What costs am I entitled to when a mandatory final offer on my Queensland motor accident claim is accepted (Motor Accident Insurance Regulation 2018, s 29)?
GIVEN `the amount of the accepted mandatory final offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the mandatory final offer, in Australian dollars
      `the offer was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mandatory final offer was accepted
      `the lower offer limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The lower offer limit fixed by the Minister under s 100A of the Act for the time of the offer, in dollars
      `the upper offer limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The upper offer limit fixed by the Minister under s 100A of the Act, in dollars
      `the declared costs limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The declared costs limit fixed by the Minister under s 100A of the Act, in dollars
      `my item 1 costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Your costs allowable under the Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 1999, schedule 2, part 2, item 1, in dollars
      `my item 5 costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Your costs allowable under the Uniform Civil Procedure Rules 1999, schedule 2, part 2, item 5, in dollars
      `the minutes my lawyer represented me at the compulsory conference` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes a lawyer represented you at the compulsory conference (0 if you had no lawyer there)
      `my costs of an application to the court` IS A NUMBER @desc Your costs of an application to the court, in dollars (0 if none)
      `my reasonable disbursements with documentary evidence` IS A NUMBER @desc Your reasonable disbursements (out-of-pocket outlays) for which documentary evidence is available, in dollars
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
DECIDE `What costs do I get on accepting a mandatory final offer` IS
    CONSIDER `the s 29 costs entitlement` `the amount of the accepted mandatory final offer` `the lower offer limit` `the upper offer limit` `the offer was accepted` `the declared costs limit` `my item 1 costs` `my item 5 costs` `the minutes my lawyer represented me at the compulsory conference` `my costs of an application to the court` `my reasonable disbursements with documentary evidence`
    WHEN JUST n THEN `I am entitled to costs of (s 29)` n
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 29 does not set my costs: the offer was not accepted, or was not more than the lower offer limit, or was more than the upper offer limit`

§§ `Attending an examination (s 30)`
-- Arises only if you are required to attend an examination in a special investigation under Part 5B of the Act.

@export Am I entitled to allowances and expenses for attending an examination under Part 5B of the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld)?
GIVEN `I am required to attend for examination under Part 5B of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an investigator has required you to attend for examination in a special investigation under Part 5B of the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994
GIVETH AN `Examination answer`
DECIDE `Am I entitled to examination allowances` IS
    CONSIDER `entitled to witness allowances and expenses (s 30)` `I am required to attend for examination under Part 5B of the Act`
    WHEN JUST x THEN `yes: allowances and expenses on the same basis as a District Court witness (s 30)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 30 does not say: it covers only a person required to attend for examination under Part 5B of the Act`
